`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
SwiftUI's `.listStyle(.sidebar)` on macOS applies system-controlled foreground colors to `DisclosureGroup` labels — they often render as `.tertiary` by default. Explicitly adding `.foregroundStyle(.primary)` overrides this so section headers appear prominently, matching the SimpleSidebar reference. The native selection highlight (accent-blue rounded fill) comes "free" from `List(selection:)` + `.listStyle(.sidebar)` + `.tag()` — but only if no `listRowBackground` override intercepts it.
